## Homage to the Blessed One, the Worthy One, the Rightly Self-Awakened One.
## The Treatise of Saddanīti (Padamālā)
## Introductory Discourse

In this world, by knowing the pure Dhamma taught by the Buddha, who is the guide for the three classes of beings, the wise realize the Deathless state (Nibbāna).

Having bowed to that Great Hero, the All-Knowing One, the Leader of the World, the Greatly Compassionate, the Most Excellent, the Pure One who bestows purity;

And having honored His pure, peaceful, unconditioned Dhamma, which is beyond the reach of mere reasoning, well-analyzed, sweet, and secure;

And having paid homage with joined palms to the Saṅgha, who is like a field for planting seeds of merit, endowed with the quality of 'tādi' (equanimity), and radiant with the pure virtues of morality, concentration, and wisdom;

By the power of the merit such as this homage performed towards the Triple Gem, having entirely removed all obstacles, I shall speak the Saddanīti—unconfused and for the benefit of the Dispensation (Sāsana) of the Teacher, who is skilled in discerning cause and effect in the world and who leads to the True Dhamma.

The fulfillment of the Dispensation occurs through the attainment of the Fruition of Arahantship, which is the destruction of the taints (āsavas). The attainment of the destruction of the taints has its root cause in the Path-knowledge that penetrates the Four Noble Truths.
